window.ScripturaLexicons.BDAG_PART_0285 = {"source":"BDAG","searchAnchorId":"bdag-search-anchor","entryAnchorId":"bdag-entry-anchor","rowsHtml":"<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-01\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"περυσινός, ή, όν adjetivo do ano passado; do ano anterior BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">περυσινός, ή, όν</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>do ano passado; do ano anterior</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-02\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πεσεῖν, -ών, πεσοῦμαι remissão verbal ver πίπτω BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πεσεῖν, -ών, πεσοῦμαι</td><td>remissão verbal</td><td>ver πίπτω</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-03\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πέταλον, ου, τό substantivo neutro lâmina; faixa de cabeça sacerdotal BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πέταλον, ου, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>lâmina; faixa de cabeça sacerdotal</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-04\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πετάομαι verbo voar; esvoaçar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πετάομαι</td><td>verbo</td><td>voar; esvoaçar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-05\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πετεινόν, οῦ, τό substantivo neutro ave; pássaro BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πετεινόν, οῦ, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>ave; pássaro</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-06\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πέτομαι verbo voar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πέτομαι</td><td>verbo</td><td>voar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-07\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πέτρα, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino rocha; maciço rochoso; pedra de tropeço BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πέτρα, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>rocha; maciço rochoso; pedra de tropeço</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-08\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"Πέτρος, ου, ὁ nome próprio masculino Pedro; sobrenome de Simão, apóstolo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">Πέτρος, ου, ὁ</td><td>nome próprio masculino</td><td>Pedro; sobrenome de Simão, apóstolo</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-09\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πετρώδης, ες adjetivo rochoso; pedregoso BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πετρώδης, ες</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>rochoso; pedregoso</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-10\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"Πετρώνιος, ου, ὁ nome próprio masculino Petrônio BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">Πετρώνιος, ου, ὁ</td><td>nome próprio masculino</td><td>Petrônio</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-11\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πεφίμωσο remissão verbal ver φιμόω BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πεφίμωσο</td><td>remissão verbal</td><td>ver φιμόω</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-12\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πήγανον, ου, τό substantivo neutro arruda BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πήγανον, ου, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>arruda</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-13\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πηγή, ῆς, ἡ substantivo feminino fonte; nascente; origem BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πηγή, ῆς, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>fonte; nascente; origem</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-14\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πήγνυμι verbo fixar; erguer; coagular BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πήγνυμι</td><td>verbo</td><td>fixar; erguer; coagular</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-15\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πηδάλιον, ου, τό substantivo neutro leme; remo de direção BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πηδάλιον, ου, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>leme; remo de direção</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-16\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πηδάω verbo saltar; saltitar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πηδάω</td><td>verbo</td><td>saltar; saltitar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-17\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πηλίκος, η, ον pronome correlativo; adjetivo quão grande; quão importante BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πηλίκος, η, ον</td><td>pronome correlativo; adjetivo</td><td>quão grande; quão importante</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-18\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πήλινος, η, ον adjetivo feito de argila; de barro BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πήλινος, η, ον</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>feito de argila; de barro</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-19\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πηλός, οῦ, ὁ substantivo masculino argila; barro; lama BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πηλός, οῦ, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>argila; barro; lama</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0285-20\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πήρα, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino bolsa de viagem; alforje; bolsa de mendigo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πήρα, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>bolsa de viagem; alforje; bolsa de mendigo</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>","cardsHtml":"<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-01\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">περυσινός, ή, όν</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">περυσινός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ή</span>, <span class=\"greek\">όν</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πέρυσι</span>; Aristoph., Pla., X. e outros; PSI 560, 8 [III a.C.]; PTebt 112, 19 [II a.C.]; também em papiros), do ano passado: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">περυσινὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὅρασις</span> «a visão do ano anterior» Hv 2, 1, 1; cf. 3, 10, 3.—DELG e M-M s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πέρυσι</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-02\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πεσεῖν, -ών, πεσοῦμαι</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>remissão verbal</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πεσεῖν</span>, -<span class=\"greek\">ών</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πεσοῦμαι</span>: veja <span class=\"greek\">πίπτω</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-03\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πέταλον, ου, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πέταλον</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (com vários significados desde Hom.; também LXX; TestSol 4:14, 16 D; TestLevi 8:2; Philo, Joseph.), literalmente «folha»; aqui, lâmina, faixa para a cabeça, usada por um sacerdote como símbolo de seu ofício: <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἱερέως</span> GJs 5:1 (duas vezes; cf. Ex 28:36; Lev 8:9).</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-04\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πετάομαι</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πετάομαι</span> (forma duvidosa em lugar de <span class=\"greek\">ποτάομαι</span> [«voar de um lado para outro, esvoaçar»], forma frequentativa de <span class=\"greek\">πέτομαι</span> [veja esse verbete].—Lob. sobre Phryn. p. 581; B-D-F §101 p. 54; Helbing 83s.; Reinhold 100.—A forma ativa <span class=\"greek\">πετάω</span> = «voar» em Achmes 236, 6. <span class=\"greek\">πετάομαι</span> em Aristot., Metaph. 1009b, 38 [WChrist ’38], variante textual [interpretação falsa, veja L-S-J-M]; Syntipas 79, 28, variante textual), estar em voo, voar; em nossa literatura, somente em Rv e no particípio presente <span class=\"greek\">πετώμενος</span>, como variante textual em 4:7; 8:13; 14:6; 19:17.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-05\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πετεινόν, οῦ, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πετεινόν</span>, <span class=\"greek\">οῦ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πέτομαι</span>), neutro substantivado de <span class=\"greek\">πετεινός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ή</span>, <span class=\"greek\">όν</span> (Theognis, trágicos, Hdt. e outros; LXX; TestLevi 9:13; Jos., Ant. 2, 245; 3, 137), qualquer espécie de ave (selvagem ou doméstica), ave, pássaro, B 11:3 (Is 16:2). Principalmente no plural (Hdt.; O. Wilck II, 1523 [127 a.C.]; LXX; En 7:5; PsSol 5:9; TestSol C prol. 3; TestJob 27:1; ParJer; Jos., Ant. 8, 40; SibOr 3, 224) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.13.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 13:4</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.4.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 4:4</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.12.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 12:24</a>. Com <span class=\"greek\">κτήνη</span> (Gen 8:17; Lev 7:26), Hs 9, 1, 8; 9, 24, 1. Com <span class=\"greek\">τετράποδα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἑρπετά</span>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.10.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 10:12</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.1.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 1:23</a>. Com <span class=\"greek\">τετράποδα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">θηρία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἑρπετά</span> (Herm. Wr. 1, 11b), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.11.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 11:6</a>; e com outros ainda, PtK 2 p. 14, 17. Com <span class=\"greek\">θηρία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἑρπετά</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἐνάλια</span>, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.3.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 3:7</a>. Com <span class=\"greek\">θηρία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἰχθύες</span>, B 6:12, B 18 (veja <span class=\"greek\">ἑρπετόν</span> quanto a essas combinações). <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανοῦ</span> (veja <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανός</span> 1d), «as aves do céu» = aves selvagens, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.6.26\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 6:26</a>; 8:20; 13:32 (cf. 1QH 8:9); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.4.32\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 4:32</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:5</a>; 9:58; 13:19; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.10.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 10:12</a>; 11:6; B 6:12 (Gen 1:28), 18; Hs 9, 24, 1; GJs 3:2; 18:2, códices. Acerca de aves de rapina, B 10:10.—BHHW III 2111. DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πέτομαι</span>. M-M s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πετεινός</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-06\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πέτομαι</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πέτομαι</span> (Hom.+; inscrições, papiros, LXX; ParJer; ApcSed 8:3 p. 132, 28 Ja.; Philo, Gig. 6; Hecataeus: 264 Fgm. 21, 203 Jac. [em Jos., C. Ap. 1, 203]. Veja <span class=\"greek\">πετάομαι</span>.), com o aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπετάσθην</span> derivado de <span class=\"greek\">πεταζω</span> (cf. Aristot., HA 624b, 6 [<span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πετάσθη</span>]; também Is 11:14; JosAs 16 cód. A [p. 65, 11 Bat.]), voar, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.4.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 4:7</a>; 8:13; 12:14; 14:6; 19:17. Aoristo, 3.ª pessoa do singular, GJs 9:1, variante textual (códices Tdf., em lugar de <span class=\"greek\">ἐπεστάθη</span>).—B. 682. DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-07\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πέτρα, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Hom. [<span class=\"greek\">πέτρη</span> como «pedra maciça», Il. 15, 273; Od. 10, 87s.]+; empréstimo no rabínico).<br>① Rocha firme ou formações rochosas maciças, rocha, diferentemente de pedras (veja 2 abaixo).<br>ⓐ Literalmente, acerca da rocha em que se escava um sepulcro (veja <span class=\"greek\">λατομέω</span> 1), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.27.60\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 27:60</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.15.46\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 15:46</a>. As rochas se fendem durante um terremoto, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.27.51\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 27:51</a> (cf. PGM 12, 242). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτραι</span> com <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὄρη</span> (PGM 13, 872, todos os elementos ficam em desordem) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.6.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 6:16</a>; semelhantemente, v. 15, onde <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> assume antes o sentido de gruta rochosa (como Il. 2, 88; 4, 107; Soph., Phil. 16 e outros; Judg 15:13; 1 Km 13:6; Is 2:10; Pr 30:26. Cf. Diod S 5, 39, 5 <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ταῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κοίλαις</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτραις</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">σπηλαίοις</span>). <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> «terreno rochoso com fina camada de terra superficial» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:6</a>, 13 (Maximus Tyr. 20, 9g <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πετρῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">σπείρεις</span>; Pla., Leg. 8, 838e; Ael. Aristid. 46 p. 302 D.; PSI 433, 6 [260 a.C.] <span class=\"greek\">οὐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐφυτεύθη</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρας</span>). Constitui alicerce adequado para construir uma casa, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.7.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 7:24</a>s.; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.6.48\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 6:48a</a>b, variante textual.—Empregado com adjetivo: acerca do Sinai, <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἔρημος</span> «rocha deserta, estéril» B 11:3 (Is 16:1). <span class=\"greek\">στερεὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> B 5:14; 6:3 (ambos Is 50:7; cf. En 22:1; 26:5; OdeSol 11:5). <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἰσχυρά</span> 11:5 (Is 33:16). <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἀκίνητος</span> IPol 1:1.—A rocha na visão de Hermas: Hs 9, 2, 1s.; 9, 3, 1; 9, 4, 2; 9, 5, 3; 9, 9, 7; 9, 12, 1 (a interpretação); 9, 13, 5; 9, 14, 4.—A rocha em vários pontos do deserto, da qual Moisés fez sair água ao golpeá-la (Ex 17:6; Num 20:8ss.; Ps 77:15s., 20; Philo, Mos. 1, 210; Jos., Ant. 3, 86; Just., D. 86, 1; Mel.—Apollon. Rhod. 4, 1444–46: Héracles, quando tinha sede, golpeou uma <span class=\"greek\">πέτρη</span> por sugestão de uma divindade, e imediatamente jorrou uma grande corrente de água). Paulo a denomina <span class=\"greek\">πνευματικὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.10.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 10:4a</a> e a identifica com o Cristo preexistente, v. 4b (EEllis, JBL 76, ’57, 53–56; Philo, Leg. All. 2, 86 <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> = <span class=\"greek\">σοφία</span>, Det. Pot. Ins. 118 = <span class=\"greek\">λόγος</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῖος</span>).<br>ⓑ Em jogo de palavras (como símbolo de firmeza, Reader, Polemo p. 265) com o nome <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span> (GGander, RTP n.s. 29, ’41, 5–29). O apóstolo assim denominado, ou a declaração que acaba de fazer, é a rocha sobre a qual Cristo edificará sua igreja (quanto à figura, veja Od. 17, 463: Antínoo não consegue abalar Odisseu, que permanece firme como rocha.—Arrian, Anab. 4, 18, 4ss.; 4, 21, 1ss.; 4, 28, 1ss.: <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> é um distrito rochoso [assim também Antig. Car. 165], fundamento de uma posição inexpugnável ou de uma fortaleza rochosa; 4, 28, 1; 2: esse tipo de <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> não poderia ser conquistado nem mesmo por Héracles.—Diod S 19, 95, 2 e 4; 19, 96, 1; 19, 97, 1 e 2; 19, 98, 1 e outros: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> [sempre com artigo] é a rocha [Petra] que protege os nabateus contra todos os ataques inimigos; Stephan. Byz. s.v. <span class=\"greek\">Στάσις</span>: <span class=\"greek\">πόλις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρης</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγάλης</span>, acerca de uma cidade que não pode ser tomada), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:18</a> (veja ADell, ZNW 15, 1914, 1–49; 17, 1916, 27–32; OImmisch, ibid. 17, 1916, 18–26; Harnack, SBBerlAk 1918, 637–54; 1927, 139–52; RBultmann, ZNW 19, 1920, 165–74, ThBl 20, ’41, 265–79; FKattenbusch, Der Quellort der Kirchenidee: Festgabe für Harnack 1921, 143–72, Der Spruch über Pt. u. d. Kirche bei Mt: StKr 94, 1922, 96–131; SEuringer, D. Locus Classicus des Primates: AEhrhard Festschr. 1922, 141–79; HDieckmann, Die Verfassung der Urkirche 1923; JJeremias, <span class=\"greek\">Αγγελος</span> II 1926, 108–17; ECaspar, Primatus Petri 1927; KGoetz, Pt. als Gründer u. Oberhaupt der Kirche 1927; JGeiselmann, D. petrin. Primat (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:17</a>ss.) 1927; BBartmann, ThGl 20, 1928, 1–17; HKoch, Cathedra Petri 1930; TEngert, «Tu es Pt»: Ricerche relig. 6, 1930, 222–60; FSeppelt, Gesch. d. Papsttums I ’31, 9–46; JTurmel, La papauté ’33, 101ss.; VBurch, JBL 52, ’33, 147–52; JHaller, D. Papsttum I ’34, 1–31; ACotter, CBQ 4, ’42, 304–10; WKümmel, Kirchenbegr. u. Gesch.-bewusstsein in d. Urgem. u. b. Jesus: SymbBUps 1, ’43; OSeitz, JBL 69, ’50, 329–40. OCullmann, TManson mem. vol., ’59, 94–105; OBetz, ZNW 48, ’57, 49–77; cf. 1QH 6:26–28; HClavier, Bultmann Festschr., ’54, 94–107.—OCullmann, TW VI 94–99: <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span>. Veja também a bibliografia sob <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span>, no final).<br>② Fragmento de rocha, pedra (em citação do OT, na qual <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> é empregada em paralelismo com <span class=\"greek\">λίθος</span>): <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">σκανδάλου</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.9.33\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 9:33</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.2.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pt 2:8</a> (ambos Is 8:14).—B. 51. DELG. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-08\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">Πέτρος, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>nome próprio masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέτρος</span> = «pedra», Hom.+; Jos., Bell. 3, 240, Ant. 7, 142.—<span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. como nome dificilmente pode ser anterior ao cristianismo, como pretende AMerx, D. vier kanon. Ev. II/1, 1902, 160ss., referindo-se a Jos., Ant. 18, 156 [Niese não aceitou a variante textual <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span> em lugar de <span class=\"greek\">Πρῶτος</span>]; mas veja ADell [<span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> 1b], especialmente 14–17. Desde o princípio, provavelmente foi considerado equivalente grego do aramaico <span class=\"hebrew\" dir=\"rtl\">כֵּיפָא</span> = <span class=\"greek\">Κηφᾶς</span>: <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.1.42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 1:42</a>; cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:18</a> e JWackernagel, Syntax II2 1928, 14s.; talvez formado por analogia com o nome próprio grego masculino <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρων</span>: UPZ 149, 8 [III a.C.]; 135 [78 a.C.]; Plut., Mor. 422d.—Um não judeu chamado <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span> em Damasc., Vi. Isid. 170. Veja também o Praeses Arabiae dos anos 278/79 d.C., Aurelius P.: Publ. Princeton Univ. Arch. Expedition to Syria III A, 1913, 4 n.º 546).<br>Pedro, sobrenome do chefe do círculo dos Doze Discípulos, originalmente chamado Simão. Seu pai chamava-se João (veja <span class=\"greek\">Ἰωάννης</span> 4) ou Jonas (veja <span class=\"greek\">Ἰωνᾶς</span> 2). Segundo <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.1.44\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 1:44</a>, ele próprio era de Betsaida; contudo, quando encontrou Jesus, vivia em Cafarnaum (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:21</a>, 29). Nessa cidade, ele e seu irmão André ganhavam a vida como pescadores (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:16</a>). Era casado (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:30</a>; cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.9.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 9:5</a>), mas abandonou lar e ocupação quando Jesus o chamou a segui-lo (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.1.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 1:18</a>; 10:28). Pertencia aos três ou quatro companheiros mais íntimos do Mestre (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.5.37\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 5:37</a>; 9:2; 13:3; 14:33). Ocupa o primeiro lugar nas listas dos apóstolos (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:2</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.3.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 3:16</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.6.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 6:14</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.1.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 1:13</a>).<br>Ainda não foram solucionados todos os problemas relacionados à atribuição do nome Cefas-Pedro a Simão (veja <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> 1), tanto a concessão de um novo nome quanto sua motivação: Platão (veja <span class=\"greek\">ὀνομάζω</span> 1) e Teofrasto [Vi. Platonis 2 linha 21 em Biog. p. 388 W. = Prolegom. 1 em CHermann, Pla. VI 196 <span class=\"greek\">Θεόφραστος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">Τύρταμος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καλούμενος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πάλαι</span>, <span class=\"greek\">διὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεῖον</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">φράσεως</span> <span class=\"greek\">Θ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">μετεκλήθη</span>]; CRoth, Simon-Peter HTR 54, ’61, 91–97).<br>Pelo menos, nem sempre foi exemplo de firmeza semelhante à rocha (<span class=\"greek\">πέτρος</span> simboliza imperturbabilidade em Soph., Oed. Rex 334; Eur., Med. 28 e outros): observem-se o Getsêmani, a negação, a tentativa malsucedida de andar sobre as águas e sua conduta em Antioquia, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.2.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 2:11</a>ss., que, porém, por vezes é atribuída a outro Cefas (veja KLake, HTR 14, 1921, 95ss.; AVöllmecke, Jahrbuch d. Missionshauses St. Gabriel 2, 1925, 69–104; 3, 1926, 31–75; DRiddle, JBL 59, ’40, 169–80; NHuffman, ibid. 64, ’45, 205s.; PGaechter, ZKT 72, ’50, 177–212; mas veja HBetz, Gal [Hermeneia] p. 105s., nota 442).<br>Apesar disso, era o líder dos discípulos de Jesus e porta-voz dos Doze (por exemplo, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.18.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 18:21</a>; 19:27; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.8.27\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 8:27</a>ss.; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.12.41\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 12:41</a>; 18:28), assim como dos três mais próximos de Jesus (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.9.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 9:5</a>); mesmo os de fora o reconheciam como líder (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.17.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 17:24</a>). Destaca-se especialmente no pronunciamento de <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:18</a>. Somente no quarto Evangelho Pedro ocupa posição menos destacada do que outra pessoa, neste caso o «discípulo a quem Jesus amava» (veja Hdb., excerto sobre <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.13.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 13:23</a>).<br>Em conexão com os acontecimentos miraculosos posteriores à morte de Jesus (sobre isso, ELohmeyer, Galiläa u. Jerusalem ’36; WMichaelis, D. Erscheinungen d. Auferstandenen ’44; MWerner, D. ntl. Berichte üb. d. Erscheinungen d. Auferstandenen: Schweiz. Theol. Umschau ’44), Pedro desempenhou papel singular: <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.15.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 15:5</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.24.34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 24:34</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.16.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 16:7</a>. Foi uma das colunas da igreja primitiva (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.2.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 2:9</a> [<span class=\"greek\">Κηφᾶς</span>]). Três anos após a conversão de Paulo, em sua primeira viagem a Jerusalém como cristão, Paulo estabeleceu contato importante com Pedro, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.1.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 1:18</a>. Pelo menos até o período descrito em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.2.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 2:1</a>–10 (cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.15.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 15:7</a>), provavelmente era o chefe da comunidade ou igreja cristã primitiva. Também atuou como missionário para Israel, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.2.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 2:8</a>; cf. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.9.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 9:5</a> (<span class=\"greek\">Κηφᾶς</span>).—MGoguel, L’apôtre Pierre a-t-il joué un role personnel dans les crises de Grèce et de Galatie?: RHPR 14, ’34, 461–500.<br>Em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1PE.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Pt 1:1</a> e <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 1:1</a> figura como autor de uma epístola. Sobre a viagem de Paulo a Roma: <span class=\"greek\">Ἀρτέμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κυβερνήτης</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλοίου</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἦν</span> <span class=\"greek\">λελουμένος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρου</span> «Ártemon, o capitão do navio, foi batizado por Pedro», AcPl Ha 7, 20. É provável que tenha morrido em Roma, sob Nero, por volta de 64 d.C.<br>No NT, por vezes é chamado <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> (veja esse verbete 1; em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.15.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 15:14</a> e <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 1:1</a>, mais precisamente <span class=\"greek\">Συμεών</span> = <span class=\"hebrew\" dir=\"rtl\">שִׁמְעוֹן</span>); com exceção de <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.2.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 2:7</a>s., Paulo sempre o chama <span class=\"greek\">Κηφᾶς</span> (veja esse verbete). Ambos os nomes: <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:16</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.5.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 5:8</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.1.40\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 1:40</a>; 6:8, 68; 13:6, 9, 24, 36; 18:10, 15, 25; 20:2, 6; 21:2s., 7b, 11, 15. <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">λεγόμενος</span> <span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.4.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 4:18</a>; 10:2. <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπικαλούμενος</span> <span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.10.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 10:18</a>; 11:13. <span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὸ</span>̔<span class=\"greek\">ς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπικαλεῖται</span> <span class=\"greek\">Π</span>. 10:5, 32.<br>Fora do NT, o nome ocorre em nossa literatura em GEb 34, 59; GPt 14:60 (<span class=\"greek\">Σίμων</span> <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span>); ApcPt Rainer; GMary 463 (2 vezes); AcPt Ox 849 (4 vezes); 1 Cl 5:4 (Paulo aparece na sequência em 5:5); 2 Cl 5:3s. (trecho de evangelho apócrifo); IRo 4:3 (<span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Παῦλος</span>); ISm 3:2 = GHb 356, 39; Papias (2:4, com outros discípulos; 15, com Marcos como seu <span class=\"greek\">ἑρμηνευτής</span>).<br>—Zahn, Einl. II §38–44; KErbes, Petrus nicht in Rom, sondern in Jerusalem gestorben: ZKG 22, 1901, 1ss.; 161ss. (contra ele AKneller, ZKT 26, 1902, 33ss.; 225ss.; 351ss.); PSchmiedel, War der Ap. Petrus in Rom?: PM 13, 1909, 59–81; HLietzmann, Petrus u. Pls in Rom2 1927; GEsser, Der hl. Ap. Petrus 1902; CGuignebert, La primauté de St. Pierre et la venue de Pierre à Rome 1909; FFoakes-Jackson, Peter, Prince of Apostles 1927; HDannenbauer, D. röm. Pt-Legende: Hist. Ztschr. 146, ’32, 239–62; 159, ’38, 81–88; KHeussi, War Pt. in Rom? ’36, War Pt. wirklich röm. Märtyrer? ’37, Neues z. Pt.-frage ’39, TLZ 77, ’52, 67–72; HLietzmann, Pt. röm. Märt.: SBBerlAk ’36, XXIX; DRobinson, JBL 64, ’45, 255–67; HSchmutz, Pt. war dennoch in Rom: Benedikt. Monatsschr. 22, ’46, 128–41.<br>—Sobre <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.16.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 16:17</a>–19, veja, além da bibliografia sobre <span class=\"greek\">κλείς</span> 1 e <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span> 1b: JSchnitzer, Hat Jesus das Papsttum gestiftet? 1910, Das Papsttum eine Stiftung Jesu? 1910; FTillmann, Jesus u. das Papsttum 1910; AKneller, ZKT 44, 1920, 147–69; OLinton, D. Problem der Urkirche ’32, 157–83; KPieper, Jes. u. d. Kirche ’32; AEhrhard, Urkirche u. Frühkatholizismus I 1, ’36.<br>—JMunck, Pt. u. Pls in der Offenb. Joh. ’50 (<a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.11.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 11:3</a>–13).<br>—OCullmann, Petrus2, ’60 (tradução inglesa, Peter, FFilson2, ’62), L’apôtre Pierre: NT Essays (volume em memória de TManson), ’59, 94–105; OKarrer, Peter and the Church: an examination of the Cullmann thesis, ’63; RO’Callaghan, Vatican Excavations and the Tomb of Peter: BA 16, ’53, 70–87; AvGerkan, D. Forschung nach dem Grab Petri, ZNW 44, ’52/53, 196–205, Zu den Problemen des Petrusgrabes: JAC ’58, 79–93; GSnyder, BA 32, ’69, 2–24; JGwynGriffiths, Hibbert Journal 55, ’56/57, 140–49; TBarnes, JTS 21, ’70, 175–79; GSchulze-Kadelbach, D. Stellung des P. in der Urchristenheit: TLZ 81, ’56, 1–18 (bibliografia); PGaechter, Petrus u. seine Zeit, ’58; EKirschbaum, The Tombs of St. Peter and St. Paul (tradução de JMurray) ’59; EHaenchen, Petrus-Probleme, NTS 7, ’60/61, 187–97; SAgourides, <span class=\"greek\">Πέτρος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰωάννης</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τετάρτῳ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Εὐαγγελίῳ</span>, Thessalonike, ’66; DGewalt, Petrus, tese, Hdlbg, ’66; RBrown, KDonfried, JReumann, editores, Peter in the NT, ’73; CCaragounis, Peter and the Rock (BZNW 58) ’89.<br>—Pauly-W. XIX ’38, 1335–61; Kl. Pauly IV 674–76; BHHW III 1430s. LGPN I. M-M. EDNT. TW. Sv.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-09\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πετρώδης, ες</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πετρώδης</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ες</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πέτρος</span> ±<span class=\"greek\">ώδης</span>; Soph. e outros), relativo a terreno rochoso com pouca terra superficial, rochoso, pedregoso (assim Hippocr., Aristot.; Jos., Bell. 7, 166, Vi. 187); substantivado, <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πετρῶδες</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.4.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 4:5</a> e <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πετρώδη</span> (Aristot., HA 5, 17) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.13.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 13:5</a>, 20; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.4.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 4:16</a>: «terreno pedregoso», sobre o qual se estende uma fina camada de terra (<span class=\"greek\">ὅπου</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἶχεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">γῆν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πολλήν</span>). GDalman, PJ 22, 1926, 124ss.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πέτρα</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-10\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">Πετρώνιος, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>nome próprio masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">Πετρώνιος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span>, nome bastante frequente (cf., por exemplo, OGI 538, 4; papiros; Philo, Leg. ad Gai. 209; Jos., Ant. 15, 307), Petrônio, centurião que comandava a guarda junto ao sepulcro de Jesus, GPt 8:31 (veja ASyn. 351, 10, onde a leitura <span class=\"greek\">Πειρώνιον</span> de Klostermann continua sem correção).—LVaganay, L’Évang. de Pierre 1930, 283s.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-11\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πεφίμωσο</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>remissão verbal</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πεφίμωσο</span>: veja <span class=\"greek\">φιμόω</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-12\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πήγανον, ου, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πήγανον</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (Aristoph. e outros; Theophr., HP 1, 3, 4; Diosc. 3, 45 e outros; POxy 1675, 4; PTebt 273, introdução; CWessely, StudPal 20 [1921], 27, 5; Jos., Bell. 7, 178; empréstimo no rabínico), arruda (ruta chalepensis: Zohary 90), mencionada entre as ervas de horta sujeitas ao dízimo, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.11.42\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 11:42</a> (o paralelo <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.23.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 23:23</a> apresenta <span class=\"greek\">ἄνηθον</span>; daí EbNestle, ZNW 7, 1906, 260s., suspeitar de uma troca de <span class=\"hebrew\" dir=\"rtl\">שברא</span> e <span class=\"hebrew\" dir=\"rtl\">שבתא</span>). Segundo a Mishná (Shebi’ith IX 1; veja Billerb. II 189), não era necessário pagar dízimo dela.—RStrömberg, Griech. Pflanzennamen ’40, 144; EBishop, ET 59, ’47/48, 81; DCorrens, <span class=\"greek\">ΧΑΡΙΣ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ΚΑΙ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ΣΟΦΙΑ</span> (KRengstorf Festschr.), ’64, 110–12.—DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-13\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πηγή, ῆς, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πηγή</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ῆς</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Hom.+; empréstimo no rabínico).<br>① Fonte de alguma coisa que jorra ou flui, nascente, fonte, fluxo (sobre a distinção em relação a <span class=\"greek\">κρηνή</span>, «fonte construída artificialmente», veja L-S-J-M, Suplemento; RWycherly, ClR 51, ’37, 2s.; Renehan ’75, 164s.).<br>ⓐ Normalmente, acerca de água, nascente, fonte, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.3.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 3:11</a>, 12, variante textual; Hs 9, 1, 8; 9, 25, 1. (<span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span>) <span class=\"greek\">πηγαὶ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span>) <span class=\"greek\">ὑδάτων</span> «(as) fontes de água» (cf. Lev 11:36; Num 33:9; 3 Km 18:5; Jdth 7:7; Ps 17:16; Jos., Ant. 2, 294; Just., A I, 64, 1) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.8.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 8:10</a>; 14:7; 16:4. <span class=\"greek\">ἀέναοι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγαί</span> «fontes perenes» 1 Cl 20:10 (<span class=\"greek\">ἀέναος</span> 1). Como típico de pecadores, <span class=\"greek\">πηγαὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄνυδροι</span> (veja <span class=\"greek\">ἄνυδρος</span>) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.2.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 2:17</a>. Acerca de uma fonte particular, poço (chamado <span class=\"greek\">φρέαρ</span> em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:11</a>s.; cf. grego moderno <span class=\"greek\">πηγάδι</span> = «poço».—WHutton, ET 57, ’45/46, 27): <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰακώβ</span>, ao pé do monte Gerizim (sobre a localização do poço de Jacó, veja Dalman, Orte3 226ss.), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:6a</a>; cf. v. 6b (Paus. 8, 23, 4 <span class=\"greek\">ὀλίγον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπὲρ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πόλιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐστιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. …).<br>ⓑ Acerca de sangue: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">αἵματος</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῆς</span> (Lev 12:7) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.5.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 5:29</a> (Alex. Aphr., An. p. 40, 2 Bruns <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">αἵματος</span>. Cf. <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">δακρύων</span>: Soph., Ant. 803; Chariton 1, 3, 6; 2, 3, 6; 6, 7, 10; Achilles Tat. 7, 4, 6).<br>ⓒ Uso fortemente simbólico (veja Hdb., excerto sobre <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:14</a>; cf. Dio Chrys. 15 [32], 15 <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">σῷζον</span> [<span class=\"greek\">ὕδωρ</span>] <span class=\"greek\">ἄνωθέν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ποθεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">δαιμονίου</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κάτεισι</span>. Em escólio sobre Pla. 611c, <span class=\"greek\">ἀθάνατος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγή</span> é uma fonte cuja água concede imortalidade) em algumas passagens do NT: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὕδατος</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ζωῆς</span> «a fonte da água da vida» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.21.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 21:6</a>; no plural, <span class=\"greek\">ζωῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηγαὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑδάτων</span> 7:17; <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὕδατος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἁλλομένου</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ζωὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">αἰώνιον</span> «fonte de água que jorra para a vida eterna» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.4.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 4:14</a> (os essênios aplicam essa figura à Torá, por exemplo, CD 6:4; veja também Hdb. ad loc.).<br>② Lugar de origem ou causa de uma plena abundância de alguma coisa, fonte originária, extensão figurada de 1 (Pind. e outros; Epict. 3, 1, 18, Apolo como <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀληθείας</span> [<span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀληθ</span>. também em Himerius, Or. 48 = Or. 14, 35; Maximus Tyr. 12, 6c; 13, 9c; Philo, Mos. 1, 84]); <span class=\"greek\">πηγὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ζωῆς</span> «fonte de vida» (Pr 10:11; 13:14; 14:27), acerca de Deus, B 11:2 (Jer 2:13 e 17:13; cf. Ps 35:10); cf. B 1:3 Funk; veja <span class=\"greek\">πλούσιος</span> 2.—B. 44. DELG. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-14\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πήγνυμι</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πήγνυμι</span>, futuro <span class=\"greek\">πήξω</span> LXX; 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἔπηξα</span>, particípio <span class=\"greek\">πήξας</span>; perfeito, 3.ª pessoa do singular e do plural <span class=\"greek\">πέπηγεν</span> e <span class=\"greek\">πεπήγασιν</span> LXX, particípio <span class=\"greek\">πεπηγώς</span> GJs, LXX. Passivo: 2.º futuro <span class=\"greek\">παγήσομαι</span> LXX; 2.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπάγην</span>; particípio perfeito <span class=\"greek\">πεπηγμένος</span> (TestJob 13:3; JosAs 2:4) (Hom.+; significado primário «cravar ou fixar em»).<br>① Tornar firme ou estável, fixando em determinado lugar, tornar firme, fixar, acerca da atividade criadora de Deus (Ps.-Lucian, Philopatr. 17 [<span class=\"greek\">θεὸς</span>] <span class=\"greek\">γῆν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐφ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">ὕδατος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔπηξεν</span>): <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐρανόν</span> «o céu» Hv 1, 3, 4 (cf. Is 42:5).<br>② Armar ou erguer uma construção, montar, construir, <span class=\"greek\">σκηνήν</span> «armar uma tenda» (Pla., Leg. 7, 817c; Polyb. 6, 27, 2; 6 e outros; Gen 26:25; 31:25; Num 24:6; Judg 4:11; Jos., Ant. 3, 247; TestAbr A 1 p. 77, 4 [Stone p. 2]); GPt 8:33; GJs 1:4. Acerca do tabernáculo (Ex 33:7; 38:26; Josh 18:1; Philo, Leg. All. 2, 54), erguer, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.8.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 8:2</a>.<br>③ Tornar sólido ou rígido, especialmente acerca de líquidos; passivo com sentido intransitivo, coagular, acerca do leite (Aristot., Part. An. 3, 15, 676a, 14 <span class=\"greek\">γάλα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πήγνυται</span>; Cyranides p. 63, 13), ApcPt Fgm. 2 p. 12, linhas 24s.; <span class=\"greek\">αἷμα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πεπηγός</span> «sangue coagulado» GJs 24:2.—DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-15\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πηδάλιον, ου, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πηδάλιον</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πηδόν</span> «pá de remo»; Hom. e outros; IG2, 1607; POxy 1449, 14; 1650, 11; latim gubernaculum «remo de governo»), pá de governo, leme, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JAS.3.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Js 3:4</a> (com <span class=\"greek\">χαλινός</span> no v. 3; cf. combinação de leme e freio em Plut., Mor. 33f <span class=\"greek\">καθάπερ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἱππεὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">διὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">χαλινοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> [<span class=\"greek\">διὰ</span>] <span class=\"greek\">πηδαλίου</span> <span class=\"greek\">κυβερνήτης</span> [HAlmqvist, Plut. u. das NT ’46, 132s.]; cf. Aristot., Mech. 5, 850b). No plural (como em PLond III, 1164h, 8 p. 164 [212 d.C.]), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.27.40\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 27:40</a>, pois cada navio possuía dois lemes, ligados por uma barra transversal e operados por um só homem (LCasson, Ships … in the Ancient World ’71, 224 nota 2).—B. 734. DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πηδόν</span>. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-16\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πηδάω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πηδάω</span> (Hom. e outros; LXX; Philo, In Flacc. 162), saltar, dar saltos, também acerca de algo inanimado (Theocrit. 25, 251); acerca de um raio de fogo (Pla., Ep. 7, 341c), <span class=\"greek\">ἀπό</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινος</span> «de alguém» ApcPt Fgm. 1 p. 12, linha 15. A menos que sigamos HSanders ao ler [<span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span>]<span class=\"greek\">πεπηδημένοι</span> AcPl BMM verso 5 // AcPl Ha 8, 33 [<span class=\"greek\">καθήμ</span>]<span class=\"greek\">ε</span>̣<span class=\"greek\">ν</span>̣<span class=\"greek\">ο</span>̣<span class=\"greek\">ι</span>̣, como restaurado pelo editor, a forma simples <span class=\"greek\">πεπηδημένοι</span> em AcPl BMM sugere uma imagem ousada de movimento rápido e, portanto, arriscado, nas «trevas da morte»; veja <span class=\"greek\">ἐκπηδάω</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πεδάω</span>.—B. 688. DELG.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-17\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πηλίκος, η, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>pronome correlativo; adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πηλίκος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">η</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> (Pla. e outros; LXX; EpArist 52; Jos., Ant. 13, 1), pronome correlativo «quão grande?», mas em nossa literatura, em ambas as ocorrências, empregado numa exclamação (em lugar do mais antigo <span class=\"greek\">ἡλίκος</span> [Pla. e outros]; veja B-D-F §304; Rob. 741).<br>① Relativo a grande tamanho, quão grande: <span class=\"greek\">ἴδετε</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλίκοις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑμῖν</span> <span class=\"greek\">γράμμασιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔγραψα</span> «vede com que letras grandes vos escrevo» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/GAL.6.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gal 6:11</a> (Dssm., B 264 [BS 358]. Contra ele, KClarke, ET 24, 1913, 285, e JClemens, ibid. 380; veja os comentários.—CStarcke, D. Rhetorik des Ap. Pls im Gal u. die ‘<span class=\"greek\">πηλίκα</span> <span class=\"greek\">γράμματα</span>’: Progr. Stargard i. P. 1911).<br>② Relativo a importância extraordinária, quão grande, extensão figurada de 1: acerca de Melquisedeque, <span class=\"greek\">θεωρεῖτε</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλίκος</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὗτος</span> «considerai quão grande deve ter sido este homem» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.7.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 7:4</a>. <span class=\"greek\">πηλίκα</span> <span class=\"greek\">μεγαλεῖα</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐδόθη</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῷ</span> «que grandes feitos (Deus) realizou (em favor de Paulo)» AcPl Ha 6, 12.—DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-18\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πήλινος, η, ον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πήλινος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">η</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ον</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πηλός</span>; Demosth. e outros; PPetr III, 48, 9 [241 a.C.]; LXX; SibOr 3, 589; Tat. 22, 1), feito de barro: <span class=\"greek\">οἰκίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. «casas de barro» 1 Cl 39:5 (Job 4:19).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πηλός</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-19\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πηλός, οῦ, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πηλός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">οῦ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (Aeschyl., Hdt.+; OGI 483, 61; CPR 232, 17; POxy 1450, 4; LXX, pseudoepígrafos, Philo, Joseph.; Mel., P. 36, 247; Ath.).<br>① Argila.<br>ⓐ Empregada na fabricação de cerâmica (trágicos e outros; Polyb. 15, 35, 2: o oleiro trabalha com <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τροχός</span> [= «roda do oleiro»] e <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλός</span>; Is 29:16; 41:25; Jer 18:6; Sir 33:13) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.9.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 9:21</a> (cf. especialmente Wsd 15:7).—Numa comparação de traços alegóricos, a humanidade é chamada <span class=\"greek\">πηλὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">χεῖρα</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τεχνίτου</span> 2 Cl 8:2 (= <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">χειρί</span>, veja <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> 1a<span class=\"greek\">δ</span>).<br>ⓑ Como material moldável empregado pelo artista (TestNapht 2:2; Jos., C. Ap. 2, 252; Mel.), a argila também é o material do qual a humanidade é feita (cf. Aristoph., Av. 686 <span class=\"greek\">πηλοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσματα</span> acerca de seres humanos; Callim. Fgm. 493; Herodas 2, 28s.; Epict. 4, 11, 27; Lucian, Prom. 13; Themist., Or. 32 segundo Aesop; Job 10:9) 1 Cl 39:5 (Job 4:19).<br>② Lama, lodo (Pla., Parm. 130c <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ῥύπος</span>; Plut., Marius 414 [16, 7], Mor. 993e; 1059f <span class=\"greek\">οἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἢ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κονιορτὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">σώματος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔχοντες</span>), especialmente a massa mole produzida quando o chão está molhado, por exemplo nas estradas (Aeneas Tact. 1421; Herodas 1, 14; Arrian, Anab. 5, 15, 2; 2 Km 22:43; Zech 9:3; 10:5; Jos., Ant. 1, 244; cf. JosAs 13:6). Jesus <span class=\"greek\">ἔπτυσεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">χαμαὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐποίησεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πτύσματος</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.9.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 9:6a</a> (<span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ποιεῖν</span> como em Chariton 1, 3, 2); cf. vv. 6b, 11, 14, 15. Sobre o emprego de <span class=\"greek\">πηλός</span> nas artes de curar da Antiguidade, inclusive por divindades benévolas, veja Hdb. ad loc. e KRengstorf, Die Anfänge der Auseinandersetzung zw. Christusglaube u. Asklepiosfrömmigkeit ’53, 39s., nota 61.—B. 20. Schmidt, Syn. II 191–99, veja <span class=\"greek\">βόρβορος</span>. DELG. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0285-20\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πήρα, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πήρα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Hom. e outros; Jdth 10:5; 13:10, 15; SibOr 6, 15; Joseph.; Tat. 25, 1), bolsa de couro usada por viajantes, alforje, bolsa de viagem, que Jesus instruiu seus discípulos a não levar quando fossem enviados, pois não era absolutamente necessária (veja <span class=\"greek\">ὑπόδημα</span>) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.10.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 10:10</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.6.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 6:8</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.9.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 9:3</a>; 10:4; 22:35; cf. v. 36.<br>Mas talvez essa instrução tenha em vista o significado mais especializado de bolsa de mendigo (Diog. L. 6, 33; inscrição grega da Síria: BCH 21, 1897, 60; PGM 4, 2381; 2400. Cf. Const. Apost. 3, 6. Tal bolsa fazia parte do equipamento de um pregador cínico itinerante [PWendland, Kultur 84. Crates, o cínico, escreveu uma obra intitulada <span class=\"greek\">Πήρα</span>: HDiels, Poetae Philosophi 1902 Fgm. 4 p. 218. Veja Dio Chrys. 49 (66), 21; Lucian, Dial. Mort. 1, 3; Alciphron 3, 19, 5].—Segundo Diog. L. 6, 13, Antístenes, o cínico, foi o primeiro a dobrar seu manto ao meio [para poder dormir sobre ele] e levar consigo um cajado e uma <span class=\"greek\">πήρα</span>; cf. 6, 22, acerca de Diógenes.—Dssm., LO 87 [LAE 108ss.]; SKrauss, <span class=\"greek\">Αγγελος</span> I 1925, 96ss.; KRengstorf, Jebamot 1929, 214s.).<br><span class=\"greek\">οἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μάγοι</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ἐξέβαλον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πήρας</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">δῶρα</span> GJs 21:3 (segundo <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.2.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 2:11</a>).—Tal bolsa também era usada por pastores (Ammon. Gramm. [I/II d.C.], diff. 112 <span class=\"greek\">πήρα</span> … <span class=\"greek\">φέρουσιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">οἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ποιμένες</span>; Longus 1, 13, 1; 3, 15, 3; Aesop, Fab. 31b H. [veja H-H. 24 II app.]; Babr. 86, 2; Jos., Ant. 6, 185 <span class=\"greek\">π</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ποιμενική</span>; veja a estátua do Bom Pastor no Laterano) Hv 5:1; Hs 6, 2, 5; 9, 10, 5.—DELG. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>"};
